{{!
    @template local_eventcalendar/access_group

    Block of access conditions (a card) in the accessrules.php page, rendered by the
    local_eventcalendar/access_rules module.

    Blocks are combined with OR and the conditions of a block with AND; the separators are written by
    JavaScript, so the card has no title.

    The X button removes the block with all its conditions. The add button is always the last element of
    the card; conditions are inserted in the "rules" region above it.

    The spacing classes come from the plugin styles.css, the same in Bootstrap 4 and 5. The card is a
    group for assistive technologies; its accessible name (with the position) is set by the JavaScript.

    Example context (json):
    {
    }
}}
<div class="card mb-2" data-region="group" role="group">
    <div class="card-body d-flex align-items-start local-eventcalendar-gap-sm">
        <div class="flex-grow-1">
            <div data-region="rules"></div>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-action="add-rule">
                {{#str}}accessaddrule, local_eventcalendar{{/str}}
            </button>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-link text-danger p-0 local-eventcalendar-push-end" data-action="remove-group"
                title="{{#str}}accessremovegroup, local_eventcalendar{{/str}}">
            {{#pix}}e/cancel, core, {{#str}}accessremovegroup, local_eventcalendar{{/str}}{{/pix}}
        </button>
    </div>
</div>
